### 4. Exclusion List

**Do NOT include:**

- Comparisons of specific AI tools (ChatGPT vs. Claude vs. Gemini vs. Copilot) — Robin explicitly declined to recommend specific tools and told listeners to match tools to their existing platform.
- Deep technical explanations of LLM architecture beyond the asterisk/probability framing Robin gave — the target audience does not need it and Robin did not develop it.
- The argument that AI will replace jobs — the article's thesis directly inverts this.
- ROI claims, time-savings percentages, or cost reduction projections — none appear in the transcript and inventing them would undermine credibility.
- AI ethics as a standalone topic — the insurance bias story is present as a human-in-loop argument, not an ethics treatise. Do not expand it into a DEI discussion the transcript does not support.
- Technical orchestration framework comparisons (LangChain, AutoGen, CrewAI, etc.) — Robin named Claude Code/Co-work as a personal favorite but explicitly did not prescribe tools.
- Generic "AI is transforming business" framing — the article's value is its specificity. Generic framing would hollow it out.

